  "schema": "ledgerloop",
  "edge_schema": "ledgerloop_edge_saas",
  "prompt": "Nele, the growth marketing manager, is planning the 2026 acquisition campaigns for each segment and asks how many new customer accounts LedgerLoop won in each month of 2025, January to December, against the same month of 2024. An account is new in the month of its created_at, which holds Brussels local time, so an account created before 2024 is new in no month here. Every month named here has ended, so each counts in full. Compare each segment's count in a month of 2025 with its count in the same calendar month of 2024, for each of the three segments: SMB, Mid-Market and Enterprise. A segment and month with no account created counts as 0. Return one row for each segment and month of 2025, with five columns in this order: month_start, the first day of the month; segment; new_accounts, the accounts of that segment created in that month; new_accounts_year_before, the accounts of that segment created in the same month of 2024; and change_pct, new_accounts minus new_accounts_year_before, as a percentage of new_accounts_year_before (12.5 for 12.5%), rounded to 1 decimal, and missing when new_accounts_year_before is 0. Sort by month_start from oldest to newest, then by segment from A to Z.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "month_start",
        "type_class": "temporal"
      },
      {
        "name": "segment",
        "type_class": "text"
      },
